.TH KITR 1 "2026-10-22" "kitr 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kitr \- early Linux/X11 Rust port of the kitty terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kitr
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-e\fR|\fB\-\-\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
.br
.B kitr
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB\-c\fR \fISCRIPT\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kitr
is a terminal emulator and behavioural port of kitty written in Rust. This
manual documents the command-line interface of the current early port.
.PP
With no command, \fBkitr\fR runs \fB$SHELL\fR (or \fB/bin/sh\fR). The GUI
frontend is used automatically when \fB$DISPLAY\fR is set and
\fB\-\-dump\-screen\fR was not requested; otherwise the headless PTY runner is
used. Use \fB\-\-headless\fR or \fB\-\-gui\fR to force a frontend.
.PP
Wayland and macOS (Cocoa) backends, tabs and layouts, kitty graphics images,
remote control and kittens are not implemented in this port.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Force the headless PTY runner. This frontend does not open a window.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Force the Linux/X11 + EGL GUI frontend. This requires a working X11 display,
EGL, and system fonts.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Load configuration from \fIPATH\fR instead of the default locations. The
current port implements a subset of kitty's options; unknown options are
ignored leniently.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " COLSxROWS"
Set the initial PTY and screen size in columns and rows. Both values must be
positive integers, for example \fB80x24\fR. When omitted, the current
terminal size is used, falling back to \fB80x24\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-scrollback " N"
Set the scrollback capacity in lines. The default is 10000.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " FILE"
Use the GUI frontend, render the terminal after child output has settled, and
write a top-down binary PPM (P6) screenshot to \fIFILE\fR. The process exits
after writing the screenshot. This is intended for testing and parity checks,
not for general screen capture.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Terminate the child after \fISECONDS\fR. Fractional values are accepted. A
timed-out headless run exits with status 124. A screenshot run also writes its
screenshot when the timeout is reached.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-screen
Write the final screen contents as plain text to standard output. This uses the
headless runner unless \fB\-\-gui\fR is also given.
.TP
.BI \-\-title " TITLE"
Set the window title. This is only meaningful for the GUI frontend.
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-
Pass the remaining arguments to the child command without further option
parsing. Everything after \fB\-e\fR or \fB\-\-\fR becomes the child's
\fBargv\fR.
.TP
.B \-c
Shortcut for running the default shell with \fB\-c\fR. The next arguments are
passed to that shell. This shortcut is disabled after \fB\-e\fR or
\fB\-\-\fR.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the built-in help text and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH SHELL INTEGRATION
The package includes unmodified copies of kitty's bash, zsh and fish
integration scripts under
\fI$PREFIX/share/kitr/shell\-integration\fR and, for fish,
\fI$PREFIX/share/fish/vendor_conf.d/kitty\-shell\-integration.fish\fR. kitr
does not yet perform kitty's automatic shell-integration injection. Users can
source the scripts manually; see \fBpackaging/README.md\fR in the source tree.
No Python is required to run the files shipped in the package.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $PREFIX/bin/kitr
Launcher wrapper installed by \fBmake install\fR. It selects a usable
\fBTERM\fR and executes the real binary.
.TP
.I $PREFIX/libexec/kitr/kitr
The actual kitr executable.
.TP
.I $PREFIX/share/terminfo/x/xterm-kitty
Compiled terminfo entry, also installed under the legacy \fI78/\fR directory.
If it is unavailable, use \fBTERM=xterm-256color\fR.
.TP
.I $PREFIX/share/applications/kitr.desktop
Desktop entry.
.TP
.I $PREFIX/share/metainfo/io.github.portlandhodl.kitr.metainfo.xml
AppStream metadata skeleton.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status is the child's exit status, or 128 plus the terminating signal
when the child is killed by a signal. A timed-out headless run returns 124.
Command-line and runtime errors return a non-zero status.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
Selects the GUI frontend automatically when set.
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell started when no command is given.
.TP
.B TERM
The launcher sets \fBxterm-kitty\fR when its terminfo entry is available and
falls back to \fBxterm-256color\fR otherwise.
.TP
.B KITR_TERM
Overrides the \fBTERM\fR value the launcher tries to use.
.TP
.B KITR_REAL_BINARY
Overrides the path of the real binary executed by the launcher wrapper.
.TP
.B KITR_SHELL_INTEGRATION
If set, the launcher exports it as \fBKITTY_SHELL_INTEGRATION\fR when that
variable is not already set. Sourcing the integration scripts is still the
user's responsibility.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kitty (1),
.BR terminfo (5),
.BR tic (1)
.SH LIMITATIONS
This is an early port. Wayland and macOS support, tabs and layouts, kitty
graphics images, remote control, kittens, and automatic shell-integration
injection are absent. Screenshot comparison against C kitty is best-effort and
depends on matching fonts, font sizes, DPI, window decorations and toolkit
rendering.
